  "user_request_original": "Design a planar multilayer dielectric coating on fused silica substrate with air incidence at normal angle (0 degrees). Use exactly 24 layers in alternating sequence: HfO2, SiO2 (Lemarchand), HfO2, SiO2 (Lemarchand), HfO2, SiO2 (Lemarchand), HfO2, SiO2 (Lemarchand), HfO2, SiO2 (Lemarchand), HfO2, SiO2 (Lemarchand), HfO2, SiO2 (Lemarchand), HfO2, SiO2 (Lemarchand), HfO2, SiO2 (Lemarchand), HfO2, SiO2 (Lemarchand), HfO2, SiO2 (Lemarchand), HfO2, SiO2 (Lemarchand) (HfO2 first at air interface, SiO2 (Lemarchand) last at substrate). Optimize all 24 layer thicknesses individually within bounds 20-200 nm using gradient_thickness optimizer with perturbation bounds ±18 nm. Maximize dual-band objective: mean transmittance in 1000-1700 nm band and mean reflectance in 300-450 nm band with equal weighting. Use coherent transfer-matrix method. Total layer count is fixed at 24. Materials are hfo2 and SiO2 (Lemarchand) from the guaranteed registry.",
